Here is a taxi.
A woman is the driver.
"Good day," I say.
"Good day. What is your address?" she asks.
"My address is Nørregade number ten," I say.
"That is in the city," she says.
Copenhagen is big and beautiful.
The houses are old and nice.
"The city is lovely," I say.
"Yes, Copenhagen is a lovely city," she says.
Now I am at my new street.
"Thank you. Goodbye," I say.
